-- Compile (JS target) typeclass instances — Fenel-authored typed values
-- (Phase 3.1 of typeclass-substrate-completion, 2026-05-28).
--
-- `loadFenelModule` projects to `SpecInstance { typeName, args, methods,
-- label }`. Phase 3.2 (2026-05-29) restored the top-level `label` via the
-- loader's `label` method-field lift (byte-identical to the original TS
-- const; dev-facing string, unconsumed by dispatch).
--
-- modules-as-values Phase 2b: Compilable and Encodable declare their methods as
-- functions (`compile : CompileSource -> Result CompileError target`, `encode :
-- a -> Result String s`), so the fields hold the functions themselves, written
-- qualified (they load as `{$ref: "<bundle>.<member>"}` references).

-- Keyed by what the compiler returns: `compileFenelToJs : CompileSource ->
-- Result CompileError JsModule`, so this is `Compilable JsModule` (it was keyed
-- `JsAst`, the AST inside the module, until modules-as-values Phase 2b).
compileJsInstance : Compilable JsModule
compileJsInstance = Compilable { compile = compileJs.compileFenelToJs, label = "CompileJs — Fenel → JavaScript" }

-- Demoted Iso → Encodable (expr-substrate Phase 6c): `deserializeJsModule`
-- is the documented Phase-5 placeholder (unconditional Err), so the Iso
-- bijectivity laws are unsatisfiable — the decode∘encode round-trip refutes
-- on every sample. The instance now claims exactly what it delivers
-- (encode-only); re-promote to Iso when a real parse-side codec lands.
encodableJsModule : Encodable String JsModule
encodableJsModule = Encodable { encode = compileJs.serializeJsModule, label = "JsModule → JS source (encode-only)" }
